## Lore

Lemurians are an ancient human people who long ago remade themselves with
Biomancy, their living magic. The result is an amphibious race that still
looks human: tall, lean, strikingly handsome, with gills tucked behind the
jaw and a body that is as much at home a mile down as it is on a beach.
They age slowly, live for centuries and are schooled from childhood in
letters, mathematics and ethics.

What sets them apart is how closely they are tied to the living world.
Every Lemurian is at least a little psychic, can feel life around him, and
is accepted by most animals as one of their own. Few will eat a mammal or a
bird, most homes are shared with lemurs and other animal friends, and a
Lemurian would rather ride a beast than sit inside a machine. They carry no
bionics or cybernetics, ever.

On Rifts Earth they have taken on the role of guardians and healers of the
planet. They are open, curious and trusting to a fault, slow to look down
on anyone, and implacable toward the undead and supernatural evil that
despoil the seas.

A Lemurian takes an O.C.C. for training, skills, combat and experience.

## GM Notes

Height 5 feet +3D8 inches (1.6 to 2.1 m). Weight 100 to 220 lbs (45 to 99
kg), all muscle. Average life span 300 years, with reports of 400; most look
to be in their twenties or thirties well into their second century.

Roughly 20% of the population practice magic, and about 65% of ordinary
citizens have no combat training. NPCs range from level 1 to 8 (2D4).

Natural enemies: the undead of the Milu, the minions of the Lord of the
Deep, and the Minions of Splugorth.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'lemurian');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
